{"_data": [{"contents": [{"type": "lesson_name", "content": ""}, {"type": "unit_name", "content": "Modeling Diagrams in UML 2.0"}, {"type": "position", "content": 11}, {"type": "origin", "content": "stub"}, {"type": "lesson", "content": 2}, {"type": "level", "content": "A1.2"}], "type": "metadata"}, {"contents": [{"type": "test", "content": "false"}], "type": "achievment_test"}, {"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "These are words you use to talk about UML 2.0"}], "type": "target_word_describer"}, {"contents": [{"type": "primary", "content": "Describe common simple incidents at work in a simple spoken or written situation with a supportive interlocutor. Assess the incident of data in the macro system processes, based on the data dictionary to consolidate intervening data, based in established parameters."}, {"type": "secondary_1", "content": "Communicates effectively in English about the communicative topics for this level through the use of appropriate basic vocabulary and grammatical structures, and with intelligible pronunciation.  Recognizes basic ideas on programming tools, diagrams of cases, and data flow diagrams."}], "type": "objectives"}, {"type": "background_image", "content": "enpe8n2le02ob11re1img01.jpg"}, {"contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "Verbs with infinitives, have to, in information questions"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "We use <span class=\"strong\">have to</span> to express a strong obligation that comes from external circumstances."}, {"type": "text", "content": "<span class=\"strong\">Have to</span> in question form is used to ask if something is really necessary to be done, the structure is:"}, {"type": "text", "content": "<div class=\"center_text\"><span class=\"strong\">wh word+ do/does+ subject+ have to+ verb+?</span></div>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "Examples: </br></br><span class=\"italic\">What do we <b>have to</b> know about diagrams in UML2.0? <br /> Where <b>does</b> she <b>have to</b> look for information about the last UML version?</span>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "Notice that when you use the auxiliary in this form, <span class=\"strong\">have to</span> keeps its base form."}, {"type": "example", "content": "What do we have to consider when we talk about diagrams in UML 2.0?"}, {"type": "example", "content": "What do we have to know about those modeling ways, Lori?"}, {"type": "example", "content": "What do we have to know about that?"}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "Modeling interactions in UML 2.0"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "As UML 2.0 represents a new dimension in the Unified Modeling Language, it has new features that turned it into a more complete version."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Compared to the previous 1.5 version, the UML 2.0 makes its usage more extensive. UML 2.0 uses new features to increase the usability to be more understandable. Inside this new version we find four modeling interactions that are:"}, {"type": "text", "content": "1. <span class=\"strong\">Sequence diagram</span>: added to achieve a behavioral aim in the system with a view of the interaction between objects."}, {"type": "text", "content": "2. <span class=\"strong\">Communication diagram</span>: added as a structural interpretation of the messaging objects."}, {"type": "text", "content": "3.<span class=\"strong\">Interaction overview diagram</span> : added to describe the combination of interactions in a logic sequence."}, {"type": "text", "content": "4. <span class=\"strong\">Timing diagram</span>:  added in 2.0 UML version to specify the time restrictions on messages sent and received in an interaction."}, {"type": "text", "content": "They added all these diagrams to send and receive messages, and they are inside the objects."}, {"type": "example", "content": "The features we find in 2.0 when we are modeling interactions are four: sequence diagram, communication diagram, interaction overview diagram and timing diagram."}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "consider "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to think carefully about something"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: What do we have to consider when we talk about diagrams in UML 2.0?"}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe8n2le02ob11aud01"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "interaction "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "mutual action or influence"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: There are some features added to the diagrams in UML 2.0 that make things easier at the moment of the object interaction."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe8n2le02ob11aud02"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "modeling"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "development of models to visualize and create systems in business and IT development."}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: The features we find in 2.0 when we are modeling interactions are four: sequence diagram, communication diagram, interaction overview diagram and timing diagram."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe8n2le02ob11aud03"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "timing diagram "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "UML 2.0 diagram created to specify the time restriction on the object's messaging "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: We can model an interaction overview and a timing diagram."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe8n2le02ob11aud04"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "communication diagram "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "basic view of the messaging between objects in UML 2.0"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Modeling interactions are four: sequence diagram, communication diagram, interaction overview diagram and timing diagram."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe8n2le02ob11aud05"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "efficient "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "performing effectively without wasting time or materials"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adjective)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example:  In other words, new features in UML 2.0 were added to old concepts to make it more efficient and useful. "}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe8n2le02ob11aud06"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "Write the improvements in UML 2.0 "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Create a poster in which you show the types of diagrams available in UML 2.0."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Share your poster with your partners."}], "type": "takeaway_extension"}, {"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "I can summarize the features improved by the last version of UML."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I can give examples of the types of modeling diagrams."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I can describe the types of diagrams for UML."}], "type": "takeaway_assessment"}], "type": "sena", "labs": [{"stimuli": [{"template_override": 1, "id": 0, "_data": [], "contents": [{}], "type": "welcome"}, {"template_override": 1, "contents": [{"value": {"audiosrc": "enpe8n2le02ob11re2aud01", "images": [{"time": "0", "image": "enpe8n2le02ob11re2img01.jpg", "id": 0, "text": "<span class=\"strong\">Teacher</span>: Lori, what do we have to consider when we talk about diagrams in UML 2.0?\n<br /><span class=\"strong\">Lori</span>: We have to consider that when we talk about modeling we refer to different ways of modeling objects.\n<br /><span class=\"strong\">Teacher</span>: What do we have to know about those ways of modeling, Lori?<br />"}, {"time": "18000", "image": "enpe8n2le02ob11re2img02.jpg", "id": 1, "text": "<span class=\"strong\">Lori</span>: We model some diagrams to create interactions between the objects, to accept, and to send messages to one another. Also, to create interactions and communication among those objects, we can model an interaction overview and a timing diagram.\n<br /><span class=\"strong\">Teacher</span>: Thank you Lori. Now Dana, you know that the earlier UML version modeling interaction is different from the 2.0 version. What do we have to know about that?\n<br /><span class=\"strong\">Dana</span>: We have to know that the basic concept is the same as in the earlier version, but there are some features in UML 2.0 that make things easier at the moment of the object interaction.<br />"}, {"time": "61000", "image": "enpe8n2le02ob11re2img03.jpg", "id": 2, "text": "<span class=\"strong\">Teacher</span>: Good, Dana. Can you mention those features, please?\n<br /><span class=\"strong\">Dana</span>: The features we find in 2.0 when we are modeling interactions are four: sequence diagram, communication diagram, interaction overview diagram and timing diagram.\n<br /><span class=\"strong\">Teacher</span>: That is correct, Dana. In other words, they added new features in UML 2.0 to old concepts to make it more efficient and useful, and the four interaction diagrams use the system framework to enclose an interaction between objects. Is that clear?"}], "coverimg": "enpe8n2le02ob11re2img01.jpg"}, "type": "slideshow"}], "type": "audio", "_data": [], "id": 2, "title": ""}, {"template_override": 1, "contents": [{"value": {"video_src": "enpe8n2le02ob11re5vqz01pt1", "images": [{"time": "0", "image": "", "id": 0, "text": "Watch this video carefully. Take notes when necessary."}]}, "type": "video"}], "type": "video", "_data": [], "id": 4, "title": ""}, {"template_override": 1, "contents": [{"value": {"video_src": "enpe8n2le02ob11re5vqz01pt2", "images": [{"time": "0", "image": "", "id": 0, "text": "Watch this video carefully. Take notes when necessary."}]}, "type": "video"}], "type": "video", "_data": 